 'Methodology analysis: test readiness before demand. A request with a title but no audience, question, source boundary, date boundary, prohibited-claim boundary, or decision owner is not ready research. It still consumes clarification capacity, so it belongs in the arrival record but not in the ready-work denominator. Next, test review load. A draft leaving the researcher queue does not mean the system gained capacity: the editor may need to compare sources, inspect the Research and Blog distinction, resolve a date conflict, narrow a claim, or pause a consequential topic. Finally, test variability. Daily arrivals are uneven, and a short run of simple briefs can hide a later cluster that requires more judgment. Use medians and distributions with the raw reasons for waiting, rather than one average that erases exceptions.',
